00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:02.149 align:start position:0%
 
gloria thank you so much  for talking today  let's focus on that bombshell leak from  the supreme court were you shocked  well i was shocked by  the unprecedented leak of a draft  opinion from the u.s supreme court uh  we've never seen anything like this  before  but more importantly the shock was  that there is a majority on the u.s  supreme court who is not just going to  chip away at roe v wade  the 1973 united states supreme court  decision that found that women have a  constitutional right to legal and safe  abortions at least at certain stages of  their pregnancy but instead the majority  is going to strike it down completely  and this of course is catastrophic and  it's dangerous to the lives and the  health of women and gloria i wonder  actually when i s i saw the leak i  wondered whether it had been leaked  because people  someone wanted it out there in order to  try and stoke up enough  resistance  that the leak document might get changed  to explain it to our viewers is this the  end of the constitutional protection for  abortion perhaps forever or do you think  that the leaked document  given the reaction in the u.s might get  changed  i think it's highly unlikely that the  decision of the majority will change  it's possible is it probable  not likely  so we have to prepare for the day  when we lose the constitutional right to  choose abortion and remembering the  victims who are going to be most at risk  and those are young women those are poor  women those are women of color those are  women who are  rural women  and  those women are most vulnerable those  four categories because often they don't  have the money to travel to another  state in the united states like  california where i am now new york some  other states haven states where abortion  will remain legal because we are  pro-choice states  and so they don't have money to put  gasoline in their car if they even have  a car or to buy a train ticket or a bus  ticket they don't have money for child  care to take care of their other  children while they travel to get an  abortion so this is mandatory motherhood  this is deciding that a fertilized egg  has more rights than an adult woman and  that is dangerous it is wrong even  teenagers who get pregnant beth  and have their parents consent to get an  abortion in some of these states they  won't be able to get it  in some of these states they're even  outlawing medicaid uh medication  abortions meaning taking a pill in your  own home to self-induce an abortion  which is important because half of all  abortions in the united states are  medication abortions and they're  often to get the pill in the mail they  have to have a consultation with a  doctor online telemedicine and many  states are outlawing that that's what's  at stake um can congress simply where do  you go from here can congress simply  legislate to replicate  that constitutional protection for women  is that an option  yes beth and that's what the president  meant when he said it could be codified  the women's health protection act has  already been passed by the house of  representatives but we all know it's  unlikely to even be voted on by the  united states senate because they will  filibuster keep talking and not allow a  vote because many of the anti-choice  politicians are cowards and they don't  want people to know that they'll vote  against the women's health protection  act and so we have to fight you know who  knows maybe we're going to have to add  justices to the u.s supreme court uh you  know we're going to have to also fight  state by state i wanted to talk to you  about your story actually um because  this is personal for you isn't it you  were one of those women  and now you're very very frightened  about this happening to other women can  you briefly tell us your story  i'm more than frightened i'm angry i'm  fired up and i'm ready to go to fight to  battle and i will be speaking at the  la city hall  rally on may 14th  and they're going to be rallies all over  this country  pro-choice rallies in every state on  that date  yes it is personal for me  because i had to pay someone who was not  licensed to perform abortions after i  was raped at gunpoint in mexico when i  was on vacation there and returned to  california when i was in my 20s and  before roe v wade made abortion safe and  legal  and then  i had to  have an ambulance called be taken to the  hospital with 106 degree fever packed in  ice and that's where a nurse said to me  i hope this teaches you a lesson  meaning she was anti-choice it did teach  me a lesson but the lesson was that  abortion must be safe and legal and  affordable and available and that is why  i have been fighting uh for pro-choice  uh laws and uh to preserve roe v wade  for  all of my professional life 47 years in  law practice and even before that and we  must protect because women will die and  will be maimed by illegal abortion or be  compelled to take pregnancies to term  when they're not ready and able uh uh to  support  uh a as a child that may be born so this  is a dangerous time and we must fight  back and just to pick up something you  said you you said that one option would  be to add justices  to the supreme court is that something  that president biden  could try to do how would that work  well you know that's that's an option  it's a very difficult one it's a very  controversial one  but you know these are  extreme times and uh  and we know that  and so you know i mean how extreme does  it get  how much dream more does it get when in  some states they're even  requiring rape victims children who are  victims of incest to give birth and not  be able to get an abortion  so you know we're going to explore all  options  all options are going to be on the table  yes this is radical as the president has  said and it is radicalizing women and  girls in this nation in the way it never  has before  so get ready we're going to be exploring  all options it's not going to be just an  academic task we are going to take to  the streets we are going to take to the  courts we are going to uh go in the  court of public opinion and we are going  to do everything that is legal and not  necessarily peaceful to win our rights  and we are going to get out the vote in  every election now uh and we are going  to vote because our lives depend on it  and that is why  we will and  gloria just rode and wade roe versus  wade it seemed permanent i remember  studying it at school  uh it was past 49 years ago when you  were just a young woman did you ever  because i don't think i did did you ever  imagine it might be overturned and do  you see this as a colossal failure of  the american left of the woman's  movement do you must feel quite angry at  your country at the moment do you  well all i can say is  the anti-choice forces have not stopped  since roe v wade  in challenging it  they have filed many lawsuits some of  which have gone to the supreme court and  in every state  so they have been fighting they have  been shipping away  and now it's the ultimate time for them  uh they are people celebrating that they  get to control women and their choices  and their lives but we are going to show  them  that we have uh you know we have the  determination and the persistence we  will resist we will persist and we will  insist  that women's rights be respected  and i believe that we will win it will  be a battle but we  expect to and intend to  win this war against women thank you so  much gloria i really appreciated your  time thank you thanks for coming on the  show  anytime

